["Okay, I have this differential equation to solve: x double dot plus 3 times x dot plus 2x equals t times e to the negative t. The problem says to find a solution in the form x(t) equals u(t) times e to the negative t. Hmm, so I need to use this substitution to make the equation simpler. 

First, let me write down the equation again to make sure I have it right: 

$$
\ddot{x} + 3\dot{x} + 2x = t e^{-t}
$$

